    "case_id": "357",
    "case_summary": "A woman in her 50s presented with a 2-week history of a painful area on the right lateral chest. She was taking prednisone, 10 mg, daily and had not used any topical medications. Previous treatments included methotrexate, mycophenolate mofetil, cyclosporine, glycopyrrolate, oral antibiotics, topical corticosteroids, topical calcineurin inhibitors, and topical antibiotics, all of which were unsuccessful.\n\nExamination demonstrated a large, crusted, erythematous plaque on the right chest.\n\n- Pathology: Biopsy was previously performed (specific results not detailed in the case report).    - Images:    Image 1 Title: Treatment Response, Figure 1A    Image Description: Large, crusted, erythematous plaque present on the patient's right lateral chest.      - Laboratory Tests:    Baseline and posttreatment laboratory values were within normal limits for:    - Intact parathyroid hormone    - Ionized calcium    - Phosphorus",
